Package: repair
Title: Measurement-Error-Corrected Regression of Random Coefficients
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
    c(person("Zachary A.", "Vig", email = "zachvig@rocketmail.com",
             role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = "Co-maintainer"),
      person("Michael N.", "Hallquist", role = c("aut", "cph"), comment = "Co-maintainer"))
Author: Zachary A. Vig [aut, cre, cph] (Co-maintainer), Michael N. Hallquist [aut, cph] (Co-maintainer)
Maintainer: Zachary A. Vig <zachvig@rocketmail.com>
Description: Implements Random-Effect Prediction Adjustment for Inference in
    Regression (REPAIR), a two-stage method for estimating relationships involving
    person- or cluster-specific intercepts and slopes from Gaussian mixed models.
    Uses a modified method-of-moments correction for sampling error in these
    estimated random coefficients, adapting the measurement-error methods of
    Fuller (1987) <doi:10.1002/9780470316665>. Extracts likelihood-only predictions
    and sampling-error covariances, aligns them with unit-level data by identifier, and reports conditional
    model-based inference and analysis diagnostics. Supports adaptive step-up
    regularization and whole-unit bootstrap sampling with percentile intervals
    for complete refitted analyses.
URL: https://hallquistlab.github.io/repair/, https://github.com/HallquistLab/repair
BugReports: https://github.com/HallquistLab/repair/issues
